| F2 | open | SUGGESTION | lib/src/cli/agent_cli_tools.dart | 💡 suggestion the others stub s schema description is frozen at registration syncotherstool registers the stub once and then early returns for the rest of the session while it exists this line the description baked in by othersdescription — deferred tools not loaded config memory list … — therefore never updates after a mount the mounted name is still advertised as not loaded in the schema the provider serializes on every request an mcp server connecting later grows discoverabletoolnames the doc comment itself says an mcp server connecting later re loads it through the next rebuild but its names never enter the description — only the live listing tool name omitted reflects them nothing breaks — the mount path answers already loaded docs e10 — but the manifest text actively misleads the model about what is loaded either re register the stub with a fresh description on each rebuild the ac9 wire size pin still holds the description shrinks as tools mount or drop the frozen name list from the description and let the live listing carry it the same early return pattern is in flutter app lib services agent tool availability dart syncotherstool |
| F3 | open | SUGGESTION | lib/src/tools/availability_gate.dart | 🪶 nit stale discoverable wording in the discovery off tombstone goal 2416 renamed the vocabulary discoverable → deferred in the docs changelog the tools render and in the discovery on branch directly above is deferred not loaded — call others … — but this discovery off branch lines 302–305 still tells the model the tool is discoverable and not loaded pure wording nothing behavioral align it with the deferred vocabulary for consistency |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

